  "question": {
    "text": "A message signal of frequency <math><mn>100</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math> and peak voltage <math><mn>100</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is used execute amplitude modulation on a carrier wave of frequency <math><mn>300</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math> and peak voltage <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>400</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> . The modulation index and difference between the two side band frequencies are:"
